      "text": "To solve for the length of \\( PC \\) in the given triangle problem, we start by noting that \\(\\triangle PAB \\sim \\triangle PCA\\). This similarity gives us the following proportion based on the corresponding sides of the similar triangles:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{PA}{PC} = \\frac{AB}{CA}\n\\]\n\nGiven the side lengths \\( AB = 8 \\), \\( BC = 7 \\), and \\( CA = 6 \\), we can substitute these values into the proportion:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{PA}{PC} = \\frac{8}{6} = \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\nLet \\( PC = x \\). Then, according to the proportion, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{PA}{x} = \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\nSince \\( PA = PB + AB \\) and \\( PB \\) is the extension of \\( BC \\), we can express \\( PA \\) as:\n\n\\[\nPA = PB + AB = PC + AB = x + 8\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( PA = x + 8 \\) into the proportion, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x + 8}{x} = \\frac{4}{3}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we cross-multiply:\n\n\\[\n3(x + 8) = 4x\n\\]\n\nExpanding and simplifying:\n\n\\[\n3x + 24 = 4x\n\\]\n\n\\[\n24 = 4x - 3x\n\\]\n\n\\[\n24 = x\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of \\( PC \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
